    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0175" n="1009" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1643</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 8, 1918</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3512. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1823. Referring to your 1438, Department’s 2140 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >2340</hi>], October 22, 2 p.m., and my 1741, Embassy’s 3078, October 25, 12
                        noon.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d103-f1"/> I have to-day received the following
                    from Admiral Sims.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>The naval authorities concur in the exceptions made by the War Trade Board in
                        its general policy and listed under the headings (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>), and (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >c</hi>), paragraph 4, of cable No. 1282,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d103-f2"
                        /> together with the modification of item (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)
                        given in War Trade Board cable No. 1438 of October 28 [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">22</hi>], 1918.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
